  "contribution": {
    "summary": "Close the accepted M3-W01 numerical matrices work package by qualifying explicit LU pivot and unpivoted QR rank thresholds, a nullable 2x2 spectral condition estimate, absence of invented conditioning for unsupported inputs, and provider-free package boundaries. Observe an independent RED, 16 GREEN tests, 81 numerical regressions and managed Math.NET corroboration before completing T2, C03 and M3-W01.",
    "value": "Expose truthful finite-binary64 solve diagnostics and bound rank/conditioning claims to observed numerical contracts. Preserve the existing LU/QR and 2x2 spectrum behavior, immutable provider copies, optional Math.NET smoke and local NuGet 0.4.0-preview.4 identity without exposing unsupported full SVD.",
    "debtChanges": [
      "The C03 work package closes only the admitted finite-binary64 dense LU, Householder QR, residual solve and 2x2 spectral subset. Full public SVD factors remain explicitly deferred in the scoped decision document.",
      "The spectral 2x2 ratio is approximate and nullable; a small residual does not establish a universal forward-error bound or exact matrix rank.",
      "Unpivoted QR and partial-pivot LU use declared relative rank/pivot thresholds. Ill-conditioned or extremely scaled cases may be refused, and numerical status is not an algebraic rank theorem.",
      "Managed Math.NET 5.0.0 remains a separately qualified optional test consumer on its observed host; no native BLAS or unexecuted RID is admitted.",
      "The numerical product has no dependency on Decision, Aura or a shared Discovery implementation. Neutral attributes, generated skills and BrokerReady require their own producer and host evidence.",
      "No public NuGet feed publication is authorized. The new preview.4 package is a local qualified artifact and its NuGet manifest is verified without inventing binary provenance.",
      "The next M3-W02 work package remains not-ready; do not make the still-open M3 milestone appear complete merely because M3-W01 has closed.",
      "Retry 1 closes the M3-W01 work-package evidence gap: attach the six verified C01/C02/C03 scientific receipts to its done state before planning validation. No test, native DWF scope or scientific admission changes.",
      "Retry 2 closes the exact target-reentry gap by retiring the completed M3-W01/C03 workflow cursor through the bounded Json.EditObject operation. Source-only cursor preconditions remain unchanged; no scientific tests or claims change."
    ],
    "nextAction": "After durable success, make the next major-cycle selection between existing M3-W02 numerical/statistical coverage and separately qualified Math adoption of the neutral dw.discovery contract once the external DWF and package gates are met.",
    "achievements": [
      {
        "projectNode": "M3-W01-C03-T2-R",
        "achievement": "Demonstrate and retain an independent missing-contract RED for an optional spectral condition estimate on the existing solve result."
      },
      {
        "projectNode": "M3-W01-C03-T2-G",
        "achievement": "Introduce nullable approximate 2x2 solve conditioning and explicit unknown outcomes, retaining the prior provider-neutral bounded LU/QR surface."
      },
      {
        "projectNode": "M3-W01-C03-T2-V",
        "achievement": "Qualify 16 boundary GREEN tests, all 81 numerics tests, existing Math regressions, optional managed-provider smoke and versioned provider-free package structure."
      },
      {
        "projectNode": "M3-W01-C03-T2",
        "achievement": "Finish pivot/rank policy, scale/condition diagnostics, inverse-free solve guarantees and the explicit bounded SVD deferral decision."
      },
      {
        "projectNode": "M3-W01-C03",
        "achievement": "Complete solving and decomposition phase C03 after separate scientific contract and numeric boundary evidence for both accepted tasks."
      },
      {
        "projectNode": "M3-W01",
        "achievement": "Close all three admitted numerical matrix/provider phases while preserving the in-progress M3 milestone and planned M3-W02 work package."
      }
    ]
  },
